class LRUCache
  def initialize(capacity)
    @capacity = capacity
    @data = {}
  end

  def get(key)
    return nil unless @data.key?(key)

    @data[key] = @data.delete(key)
  end

  def put(key, value)
    @data.delete(key)
    @data.delete(@data.first[0]) while @data.any? && @data.size >= @capacity
    @data[key] = value
  end

  def size
    @data.size
  end
end
```

Uses Ruby's insertion-ordered `Hash` as the recency list: `get` reinserts the key to mark it most-recent, and `put` deletes + reinserts, evicting the oldest entry (`@data.first`) when full. Verified with a quick script: hit/miss, eviction of least-recently-used, and updates don't grow the cache. O(1) amortized for both ops.
